# Author identity map
#
# This project accumulated eight git identities across four machines and two
# institutions, three of which used strings that are not real email addresses
# ("match@Raman", "sjbrooke@matchbook", "Martin"). Git and GitHub key an author
# on their email, so those commits render as unlinked strangers.
#
# This file is the non-destructive fix: it rewrites how authors are DISPLAYED
# by `git shortlog`, `git log`, `git blame` and most tooling, without touching
# commits.
#
# What it does NOT fix: GitHub's contribution graph, which reads the raw commit
# email and ignores .mailmap. Repairing that needs a real history rewrite
# (`git filter-repo --mailmap .mailmap`), which changes every commit hash and
# forces everyone to re-clone. See MODERNIZATION.md.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Samuel Brooke — one person, six identities.
#
# Canonical address is the personal one rather than the University of Melbourne
# address, deliberately: the institutional account will not outlive the work,
# and the goal is that these commits stay attributable indefinitely.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> NanoMatch <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> Sam <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> NanoMatch1 <40452389+NanoMatch1@users.noreply.github.com>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> MelMatch <sam.brooke@unimelb.edu.au>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> nanomatch <sjbrooke@matchbook>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> samuel@imdea <samuel.brooke@imdea.org>
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> match@matchpi <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ "match@raman <match@Raman>" is a MACHINE account, not a person.
#
# It is the default identity of the lab PC in Melbourne. Every commit under it
# so far is Samuel's (137 commits, 2025-03-31 .. 2026-08-26, confirmed), so the
# mapping below is correct today.
#
# It will stop being correct as soon as anyone else commits from that machine,
# and .mailmap cannot split one identity by date. There is no way to tell from
# the commit itself which human was sitting at the rig.
#
# Therefore: anyone working on the lab PC must set their own git identity
# before committing. See docs/git_workflow.md. If this mapping ever starts
# absorbing someone else's work, delete this line rather than leaving it —
# a misattributed contributor is worse than an unlinked one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Samuel Brooke <sjbrooke1993@gmail.com> match@raman <match@Raman>

